  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Point it at a folder of per-subject standing (COP) and walking (COM) trial files from the CAVE sum-of-sines visual-perturbation protocol, and it computes gain, phase and coherence at each stimulus frequency plus RMS, path-length and velocity sway metrics, then shows them as bar, recovery-trajectory, Nyquist and spectra plots and as CSVs to download. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
